    <body period="#tg_2015">
      <section eId="sec_1">
        <num>1</num>
        <heading>Short title and commencement</heading>
        <subsection eId="sec_1__subsec_1">
          <num>(1)</num>
          <content><p>This Act may be cited as the Personal Data Act 2015.</p></content>
        </subsection>
        <subsection eId="sec_1__subsec_2">
          <num>(2)</num>
          <content><p>This Act comes into force on 1 July 2015.</p></content>
        </subsection>
      </section>
      <section eId="sec_2">
        <num>2</num>
        <heading>Interpretation</heading>
        <content>
          <p>In this Act, "controller" means a person who determines the purposes for which personal data is processed, and "personal data" means information relating to an identified or identifiable individual.</p>
        </content>
      </section>
      <section eId="sec_3">
        <num>3</num>
        <heading>Convention given effect</heading>
        <content>
          <p>This Act gives effect in Aurelia to the <ref href="/akn/xr/treaty/2010/1" ulis:relation="implements">Northern Union Convention on the Protection of Personal Data 2010</ref>.</p>
        </content>
      </section>
      <section eId="sec_12">
        <num>12</num>
        <heading>Retention limit</heading>
        <subsection eId="sec_12__subsec_1">
          <num>(1)</num>
          <content><p>A controller shall not retain personal data for longer than seven years after the purpose for which it was collected has been fulfilled.</p></content>
        </subsection>
        <subsection eId="sec_12__subsec_2">
          <num>(2)</num>
          <content><p>Subsection (1) does not apply to personal data that a controller is required to keep by another Act.</p></content>
        </subsection>
      </section>
      <section eId="sec_13">
        <num>13</num>
        <heading>Right to erasure</heading>
        <subsection eId="sec_13__subsec_1">
          <num>(1)</num>
          <content><p>A data subject may require a controller to erase personal data concerning the data subject that is no longer necessary for the purpose for which it was collected.</p></content>
        </subsection>
        <subsection eId="sec_13__subsec_2">
          <num>(2)</num>
          <content><p>A controller shall comply with a requirement under subsection (1) within thirty days.</p></content>
        </subsection>
      </section>
      <section eId="sec_20">
        <num>20</num>
        <heading>Transitional registration</heading>
        <content>
          <p>A controller registered under the Data Registry Act 1998 immediately before 1 July 2015 is treated as registered under this Act until 30 June 2017.</p>
        </content>
      </section>
    </body>
